why can't sharkboy breathe underwater  and why would supposedly valiant heroes  steal cookies here are a few things  about the adventures of sharkboy and  lava girl that people only seem to think  about once they've grown up in the mid  2000s robert rodriguez was arguably at  the height of his powers the texas-born  filmmaker had gone from producing el  mariachi for a mere seven thousand  dollars in 1992 to developing beloved  hits like desperado from dusk till dawn  and of course the spy kids films however  the adventures of sharkboy and lava girl  was undeniably a low point in the  director's career even the most inane  toilet humor-based kids movies will  often throw in some jokes for the  parents sharkboy and lava girl however  is aimed squarely at the kids and that's  because it was partially written by one  the opening titles of sharkboy and lava  girl introduce it as a rodriguez family  movie based on the dreams of  then-seven-year-old racer max rodriguez  who also played young sharkboy in the  opening scene the adults in the movie  although played by household name actors  like george lopez david arquette and  kristen davis still deliver stiff  awkward dialogue that sounds like a  child's idea of the way an adult might  speak for an adult hoping for action  like desperado a compelling narrative  like sin city or special effects like  elita battle angel sharkboy and lava  girl is certainly one of the less  compelling rodriguez films  the word dream or some variation of it  is uttered a total of 188 times  throughout sharkboy and lava girl's 93  minute run time that means the word is  being said on average once every 30  seconds but in some scenes it's much  more often than that even by the 50th  time it still isn't very clear what the  movie has to say about dreams other than  that they're a good thing to have young  max is mocked by his classmates for  reading stories about sharkboy and lava  girl from his dream journal but then his  dreams turn out to be real so linus and  the other kids learn that dreams are  good because they can become real but  max's dream almost destroys the school  and that doesn't sound very good at all  there's also the matter of max's parents  his father is an unemployed writer and  his inability to get a reliable job has  pushed his parents to the brink of  divorce at the film's climax rather than  finding some sort of mature compromise  the pair have a near-death discussion  where they remind each other that  they're best friends reconciling without  actually resolving the issue at hand  rather than have max's father figure out  a way to follow his dreams while still  supporting his family the movie just  ends sharkboy and lava girl make such a  repetitive point about the importance of  dreaming that it seems like it should  actually have something to say by the  end of it instead all this talk of  dreams eventually starts to sound more  like a nightmare  the adventures of sharkboy and lava girl  is on the one hand refreshingly colorful  and vivid during a time when even kid  targeted action movies were slowly  inching towards gloomy dystopian  franchises like the maze runner and the  hunger games the colorful world of  drools stood out as a unique vision on  the other hand when an adult watches  sharkboy and lava girl they see a film  drunk on its own green screen power one  that makes you wonder how it could have  possibly cost 50 million dollars to  produce at the time of the film's  release in 2005 cgi was being used more  and more in all sorts of movies but the  technology was at the end of an awkward  transitional phase sharkboy and lava  girl was shot almost entirely in front  of a green screen and it shows with its  more fantastical settings resembling a  window screensaver more than a major  motion picture that's not to say that  cgi heavy movies can't be good 1982's  tron and 2008 speed racer are both  underrated gems but as an adult watching  sharkboy and lava girl in 2021 it's hard  to not be distracted by visual effects  less sophisticated than an instagram  filter additionally the 3d technology  used for sharkboy and lava girl made for  a good selling point but did little to  actually make the film look good  sharkboy and lava girl utilized anaglyph  3d the kind that uses those red and blue  glasses which just made the movie look  even worse on the big screen as roger  ebert put it in his review fully three  quarters of the movie is in 3d which  looks more like 1d to me removing the  brightness and life of the movie's  colors and replacing them with a drab  listless palette which is about as  exciting as looking at a 3d bowl of  oatmeal  in 2005 george lopez was at the top of  his game he was gearing up for the fifth  season of his highly rated sitcom george  lopez he'd made cameos and shows like  curb your enthusiasm and he'd establish  himself as a well-respected stand-up  comedian in sharkboy and lava girl lopez  fully commits to his dual role as max's  teacher mr electricidad as well as one  of the chief bad guys on planet drool mr  electric both roles are over the top of  course and lopez mostly pulls them off  highlights include his demand for max  and his bully to be friends as a teacher  or his constant spouting of  electricity-based puns as a floating orb  with claws for hands  but why did george lopez also have to  provide a voice over from max's  childhood robot tobor following the  success of films like aladdin and shrek  hollywood had developed something of an  obsession with casting movie stars and  voice roles largely ignoring an entire  industry of talented voice professionals  who have been providing their talents to  cartoons and animated movies for decades  prior so rather than finding the perfect  voice actor to design an endearing  identity for tobo around the audience  gets george lopez again and yet again  for a fourth time as a guardian of the  ice princess robert rodriguez himself  even voices a talking shark further  trading creativity for mediocre  uninspired stunt casting  out of everyone in sharkboy and lavagirl  it's clear that future twilight  heartthrob taylor lautner is the actor  who possesses it that indefinable  quality that makes a movie star well a  movie star when production on the film  began lautner was just 12 years old he  already had an extensive martial arts  background earning a black belt by age 8  and appearing in a national karate  tournament in 2003. lautner was the  first and only actor to audition for the  role of sharkboy rodriguez was truly  convinced he was perfect from the very  beginning sure enough lautner sharkboy  is a glowering menace he never stops  moving in rages easily snarling and  yelling without holding back he plays an  important role in the most standout  action scene of the film using his  martial arts skills in an elaborate  fight with mr electric's dog-like cord  monsters rodriguez even asked lautner to  choreograph his own fight scenes lautner  also takes center stage for one of the  most bizarre and memorable moments of  shark boy and lava girl a ridiculous  inexplicably aggressive lullaby that he  sings to get max to fall asleep and  dream planet drool back to his rightful  shape he busts impressive dance moves  while sing yelling all sorts of absurd  lines it's a shame that taylor lautner  couldn't return for we can be heroes the  2020 quasi sequel to sharkboy and lava  girl as he was undoubtedly the true star  of the original  you'd think that the whole point of  having elements of max's dream world  echo elements of max's real world would  be to illuminate his relationships with  the people and things that surround him  lava girl for example asks max why he  made her shark boy's partner when  they're quote not compatible the same  words max's mother used to describe why  she and max's father are not getting  along such moments could if properly and  somewhat clearly presented give a film  like this greater depth unfortunately  sharkboy and lava girl breeze past the  questions as quickly as they bring it up  the additional presence of max's parents  as cookie hungry giants on planet drool  just serves to make things even more  confusing then there's mr electricidad  who allows his daughter marissa to face  off against a giant robot with his own  face on it while the idea of a girl  facing off against an imaginary  construct of her own father seems like  it could be richard symbolism such  moments don't seem to connect to any  greater theme other than revolving  around the loose freudian concept of  dreams being inherently meaningful  the adventures of sharkboy and lava girl  has a few off-putting attempts at the  sort of wink-wink adult humor of the  children's movies sometimes tackle with  wit and subtlety here however they come  across as awkward at best and just plain  confusing at worst at one point sharkboy  says he's heard that the ice princess is  the most beautiful girl on the planet  causing lava girl to get jealous and zap  him in the butt with her lava powers  other moments include mr electricity  dad's insistent that max stays away from  his daughter and linus's reaction to  lava girl burning his desk during  moments like these it feels like you can  see remnants of a screenplay with jokes  intended for adults but they're  ultimately more have baked than the  cookies in max's kitchen and we can be  heroes it is revealed that the pair  eventually got together and had a child  of their own at some point it seems that  what was once implied has now become  explicit it might seem like a minor  detail but early on in sharkboy and lava  girl max wakes up to find that the  cookies his mom baked and left in the  kitchen have been strangely consumed one  of the cookies has jagged shark-like  teeth marks in it while the other is  burnt and remains hot to the touch his  parents of course don't believe his  repeated insistence that it wasn't him  who ate the big treats and clearly  judging from the evidence it was  sharkboy and lava girl it's not until  the next day that the duo reveal  themselves as real heroes recruiting max  to help them save planet drool while  he's asleep in class as cute as the  scene might be it also begs a question  why bother sneaking into his house the  night before they were going to contact  him anyway are there heroes like santa  claus did they think it would be funny  to get max into trouble not only has max  seemingly discovered that sharkboy and  lava girl are real but in this scene he  also learns that they have no issues  with chocolate chip thievery  after he wraps up his battle with minus  on drool lava girl tells max to blink  three times which will take him home  much like dorothy clicking her heels  together in the wizard of oz when he  does so he wakes up back in his  classroom implying that a large portion  of what we've just seen was a dream of  some sort but during that dream max fell  asleep and had another dream inside of  that dream is that even possible it  seems like the adventures of sharkboy  and lava girl is a lot like inception  but without leonardo dicaprio patiently  explaining how things work there are  dreams within dreams and then those  dreams intrude on what you thought was  reality all along like dreams themselves  the whole thing is as impossible to  follow as it is to explain to anyone  else  this is yet another nitpick but it's the  sort of thing that can really nag an  adult up until the very last battle on  drool it is made abundantly clear that  sharkboy possesses the abilities of well  a shark after being lost at sea sharkboy  was raised by sharks growing sharp teeth  fins and gills as he adapted to the  shark lifestyle however in the big  showdown with mr electricidad electric  deals get the better of sharkboy nearly  causing him to drown you know because  sharks have to watch out or they could  drown  what about the gills that we saw all up  and down the sides at the beginning of  the film it's an example of a screenplay  giving a character a newfound limitation  simply because it is called for at that  particular moment to build dramatic  tension it's also frustratingly lazy  nearly two decades later the adventures  of sharkboy and lava girl continues to  hold a special place in the hearts of  those who discovered it as kids however  thanks to all sorts of bizarre moments  and choices you'd probably be doing  yourself a favor to keep the movie in  your memories rather than revisiting it  on your streaming side of choice  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

